WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.390 --> 00:00:05.430
When the intergalactic megalomaniac Thanos
came face-to-face with the quick-witted, nanotech-fitted

00:00:05.430 --> 00:00:09.891
Iron Man in Avengers: Infinity War, their
conversation didn't quite play out how fans

00:00:09.900 --> 00:00:11.220
may have expected it to.

00:00:11.300 --> 00:00:14.920
Rather than watching as the hulking purple
villain questioned who the armored Avenger

00:00:14.930 --> 00:00:20.650
was, viewers saw Thanos instantly recognize
Tony Stark by name as the man inside the red-and-gold

00:00:20.650 --> 00:00:21.150
get-up.

00:00:21.240 --> 00:00:25.080
Fans of the Marvel Cinematic Universe have
already come up with more explanations as

00:00:25.099 --> 00:00:29.769
to how Thanos seems to have known Tony prior
to Infinity War than we can count - and another

00:00:29.769 --> 00:00:32.430
intriguing idea has just been added to the
mix.

00:00:32.430 --> 00:00:36.710
Building off of what the film's co-directors
Joe and Anthony Russo previously said about

00:00:36.710 --> 00:00:41.079
the characters' relationship, one Reddit user
has theorized that Thanos and Tony actually

00:00:41.080 --> 00:00:43.100
met before the events of Infinity War.

00:00:43.320 --> 00:00:47.460
But before anyone rattles off a list of reasons
as to why that's impossible, wait until you

00:00:47.460 --> 00:00:49.080
hear the other half of the theory.

00:00:49.420 --> 00:00:53.859
The idea goes that Thanos and Tony will meet
again and fight in Avengers 4, duking it out

00:00:53.860 --> 00:00:56.620
in an encounter that technically happens in
the past.

00:00:56.760 --> 00:01:01.620
So far, most people have accepted that Thanos
recognizes Tony from the final fight in Avengers

00:01:01.620 --> 00:01:05.640
1, remembering him as one of the heroes who
stopped his original plan for gathering the

00:01:05.640 --> 00:01:08.700
Infinity Stones - even though he wasn't on
the ground to witness it.

00:01:08.740 --> 00:01:12.400
It's a perception that would seem to be bolstered
by comments from the Russo Brothers on the

00:01:12.410 --> 00:01:16.409
Infinity War commentary track, where they
said Thanos recognized Tony "from the original

00:01:16.409 --> 00:01:19.220
Battle of New York as the person who undid
the plan."

00:01:19.390 --> 00:01:23.340
But if the fourth Avengers movie really does
delve into time travel, then perhaps Thanos

00:01:23.340 --> 00:01:27.240
is remembering a Battle of New York - or some
other fight - that we don't know about yet.

00:01:27.460 --> 00:01:31.740
The theory posits that the Avengers will defeat
Thanos by travelling through time to before

00:01:31.740 --> 00:01:36.299
his Infinity War victory, doing battle with
him in the past before the events of the third

00:01:36.300 --> 00:01:37.480
Avengers even happen.

00:01:37.620 --> 00:01:41.940
Interpreted that way, Thanos in Infinity War
is meeting the Avengers again, while from

00:01:41.940 --> 00:01:44.360
their point of view, they're meeting him for
the first time.

00:01:44.540 --> 00:01:48.300
This theory is attention-grabbing for sure,
but when you take a step back and look at

00:01:48.300 --> 00:01:53.200
the Avengers 4 rumor mill as a whole, you'll
realize that the idea sounds pretty familiar.

00:01:53.500 --> 00:01:57.580
Back in June, not long after Infinity War
opened in theaters for its record-setting

00:01:57.580 --> 00:02:03.040
run, Screen Rant's Thomas Bacon posed his
own theory about Thanos, Tony, and time-travel.

00:02:03.040 --> 00:02:04.140
Bacon hypothesized,

00:02:04.360 --> 00:02:09.039
"There's strong evidence that Avengers 4 explores
the idea of time-travel, with the surviving

00:02:09.040 --> 00:02:10.860
Avengers traveling back to the past.

00:02:11.020 --> 00:02:15.440
As such, it's entirely possible that Thanos
could have met a future Tony Stark […] Going

00:02:15.440 --> 00:02:20.080
one step further, this may well explain why
Thanos snarls, 'I hope they remember you.'

00:02:20.220 --> 00:02:23.880
Perhaps he already knows when Stark will finally
die - because he's seen it happen?"

00:02:23.940 --> 00:02:27.760
While the theory has mutated a little bit
since the home release of Avengers: Infinity

00:02:27.760 --> 00:02:30.780
War, there's still enough to it to warrant
some consideration.

00:02:31.030 --> 00:02:36.260
With set photos from Avengers 4 clearly showing
battlefields from previous movies, it's totally

00:02:36.260 --> 00:02:40.989
possible that the end game will see Tony duking
it out with Thanos in an alternate timeline's

00:02:40.989 --> 00:02:41.489
past.

00:02:41.720 --> 00:02:45.980
Marvel is one of the most secretive studios
out there, so despite how spoiler-happy Tom

00:02:45.989 --> 00:02:50.120
Holland and Mark Ruffalo have been in the
past, fans shouldn't expect anyone involved

00:02:50.120 --> 00:02:54.830
with the fourth Avengers movie to start spitting
truths about this particular time-travel theory

00:02:54.830 --> 00:02:57.440
- or any other Avengers 4 theory for that
matter.

00:02:57.600 --> 00:03:01.299
For the time being, the Marvel-loving masses
can either immerse themselves in the weird

00:03:01.299 --> 00:03:05.990
and wonderful world of fan theories, believing
a new possible storyline for Avengers 4 every

00:03:05.990 --> 00:03:10.400
week - or they can take the Russo Brothers'
words at face value, and patiently wait for

00:03:10.400 --> 00:03:12.320
the answers just like everybody else.

00:03:12.420 --> 00:03:17.680
Either way, all shall be revealed when Avengers
4 opens in theaters on May 3rd, 2019.

